{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.YoungTableaux","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.YoungTableaux","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Partition","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dLambda_sq_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.sum_dLambda_sq_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L102-L119","doc":"The RSK / Burnside target restated with this file's `dLambda`: `∑_{λ ⊢ n} dLambda(λ)² = n!` is\nequivalent to `QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideHolds n`.  (This is a *restatement*, not a proof — the\nidentity itself needs the RSK correspondence, absent from the pinned Mathlib; it is the target of\nbean SW-3.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.dLambda_eq_dimSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.dLambda_eq_dimSYT","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L95-L100","doc":"`dLambda λ` (this file's `Fintype.card`) equals `QOU.Mathlib.dimSYT λ` (its `Nat.card`), so the\nSchur–Weyl-facing dimension is definitionally the same combinatorial number that the RSK/Burnside\ntarget `∑_{λ ⊢ n} dimSYT(λ)² = n!` ranges over. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.numSYT_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.numSYT_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L88-L93","doc":"`numSYT` (this file's `Fintype.card`) equals the pre-existing `numStandardYoungTableaux`\n(`QOU.Mathlib`'s `Nat.card`).  `Nat.card` and `Fintype.card` coincide on a `Fintype`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.dLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.dLambda","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L82-L84","doc":"**`dLambda λ = #SYT(λ)`** — the dimension of the Specht module `S^λ`, presented as a\n`Fintype.card` over the standard Young tableaux of shape `λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.numSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.numSYT","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L79-L80","doc":"**`#SYT` of a Young diagram**, as a `Fintype.card`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.instFintypeStandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.instFintypeStandardYoungTableau","kind":"instance","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L69-L75","doc":"SYT of any Young diagram form a `Fintype`.  The underlying type is `Finite`\n(`QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.instFinite`, via an injection into a finite function space);\n`Fintype.ofFinite` upgrades that to a `Fintype` (`noncomputable`).  This is the one genuinely new\nconstruction of this file — it is what lets `#SYT` be a `Fintype.card`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SYT","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L64-L67","doc":"A **standard Young tableau of shape `λ`** — the in-repo `QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau` of\nthe diagram `shape λ`.  Rows and columns are strictly increasing and the entries are a bijection\nonto `{1,…,n}`; see `QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.row_strict`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.shape","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L60-L62","doc":"The Young diagram (shape) of a partition `λ ⊢ n` — its parts sorted weakly decreasing as row\nlengths.  Delegates to `QOU.Mathlib.partitionShape`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.numPartitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.numPartitions","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L55-L56","doc":"The number of partitions of `n` (`p(n)`), as `Fintype.card`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.instFintypePartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.instFintypePartition","kind":"instance","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L49-L53","doc":"Partitions of `n` form a `Fintype` (Mathlib's instance; `Classical.choice`-backed, so\n`noncomputable` — it does not reduce in the kernel).  Restated here so the Schur–Weyl program can\n`∑`/`⊕` over `Partition n` without reaching into `Nat.Partition`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.Partition","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/YoungTableaux.lean#L45-L47","doc":"A **partition** `λ ⊢ n` — an abbreviation for Mathlib's `Nat.Partition n` (a multiset of\npositive parts summing to `n`).  Reused verbatim; not reinvented. ","signatureChunk":0}]}